% circular_test.glp - Tests for term operations used with circular terms
%
% NOTE: Circular terms form through cross-goal communication in MULTIAGENT
% settings. In single-agent REPL, SRSW constraints prevent direct circular
% term creation. Phase 1 unit tests verify circular term handling works.
% These REPL tests verify the helper predicates work correctly.

% Test ground guard on a value
% is_ground(Val, Result) - Result is yes if Val is ground, no otherwise
is_ground(X, yes) :- ground(X?) | true.
is_ground(_, no) :- otherwise | true.

% Test equality via =?= (both args must be ground)
% test_equal(A, B, Result) - Result is yes if A =?= B, no otherwise
test_equal(X, Y, yes) :- X? =?= Y? | true.
test_equal(_, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

% Self-equality test for a single term
test_self_equal(X, yes) :- X? =?= X? | true.
test_self_equal(_, no) :- otherwise | true.

% Helper to display a value (for testing)
show(X, X?).
